v4.5.1: harden install-cloakgpt.ps1 based on CloakGPTWindows installer patterns

- Added param([switch]$Uninstall) - same script handles install AND uninstall
- Find-CloakGPTSource: multi-path detection (script dir, all nested extraction
  permutations, Downloads folder, real Desktop + USERPROFILE\Desktop + all
  OneDrive-* variants for corporate OneDrive users, manual drag-and-drop path
  entry with quote-stripping)
- Path-filtered process kill: never touches Windows System32 svchost.exe /
  sihost.exe / dllhost.exe by checking Path starts with allowed roots
- Cooperative uninject before overwriting old C binaries (spawns old
  sihost --unload)
- Preserves config.dat / session / API keys / logs during upgrade
- Registry-backup Defender exclusions (survives if Set-MpPreference is
  blocked by Tamper Protection)
- Tamper Protection detection + clear instructions
- Verifies all 5 C binaries present after extraction (catches Defender
  quarantine mid-flight with clear "restore from Protection History" advice)
- MoveFileEx MOVEFILE_DELAY_UNTIL_REBOOT for locked-file cleanup
- Ask-Choice input validation loop
- Colored step output (Write-Ok/Warn/Err/Info/Step helpers)
- Uninstall path: cooperative uninject + Defender exclusion removal +
  install-dir wipe + shortcut removal + optional reboot for locked files

Compatibility: pure PowerShell 5.1 (Windows 10 default). ASCII-only, verified
0 non-ASCII bytes. Syntax-validated via [System.Management.Automation.Language.Parser].
E2E tested: installer deleted all 5 C binaries, svchelper on next launch
re-copied them from bundle within 6 seconds.

Reference: mirrored the robust patterns from
C:\Users\<you>\Desktop\CloakGPTWindows\install.ps1 (CloakGPT v5.3 installer).
